--- body ---
## Context
A session on 2026-10-21 asked whether the harness has smart testing (diff analysis,
coverage map, red/green cache). Findings, measured or sampled in that session:
- Three partial mechanisms exist (testmon helper, `scoped-check`, review evidence)
  with no shared key; only the harness repo has the testmon helper wired.
- `rules/coding-python.md` and `skills/hunt` instruct agents unconditionally to use
  the testmon helper. For suites that read files, shell out or use data, an
  undeclared read gives a stale green; two sibling projects have 54 and 12
  subprocess-spawning test files and 214 and 67 file-reading ones.
- The useful interventions found were project-specific and cheap (a serial fast
  tier that never used the worker plugin it already depends on; one 45 s test on the
  fast path; a worktree measured without its data deselecting 750 tests instead of
  81, which made a 272 s tier look like 12.6 s). A recipe cannot carry that; a
  consultation can.
- Session traces carry timestamps on tool calls and results, so command wall time
  is derivable (827 test/gate calls in 400 traces, 615 paired).

Author decision: do not instruct agents unconditionally; build a testing expert,
modelled on a doctor's visit, never called automatically. At `lair` a script
reflects on speed bumps and suggests calling the expert.

## Scope
- `skills/pulse/`: the consultation (intake, chart review, examination, differential,
  confirmation, treatment plan, intervention, follow-up), with references for the
  usual syndromes and the toolkit. `disable-model-invocation: true`.
- `scripts/pulse_traces.py` (collect, survey) and `scripts/pulse_profile.py`
  (profile with a worker bound, compare): standard-library evidence tools.
- Wording removal: `rules/coding-python.md` and `skills/hunt` stop instructing the
  testmon helper; it stays available as one remedy the expert may propose.
- `lair`: a report-only step that runs the survey and suggests the consultation.
- Not in scope: gate semantics, `/verify-gate`, any change to a project's targets.

## Exit criteria
- [x] `rules/coding-python.md` and `skills/hunt/SKILL.md` no longer tell agents to run the testmon helper; a test pins the absence
- [x] `/pulse` exists, is not model-invocable, and its first sentence is plain function; catalog regenerated, drift clean
- [x] The consultation covers history, symptoms, triage, evidence by script, diagnosis, remediation and verification by re-measurement or simulation; tests pin the contract
- [x] `pulse_traces.py survey` fires on a synthetic slow-gate trace (positive control), stays silent on a clean one, and says "not checked" when it cannot look
- [x] `pulse_profile.py` reproduces a known tail concentration and its worker lower bound from a fixture
- [x] `lair` suggests the consultation from the survey, never runs it
- [x] `make check` passes; adherence self-gate recorded; PR under the 15-file breaker, else split
